
## ✅ Correct way to remove it (Flatpak)

### 1️⃣ Check if it’s installed via Flatpak as like "workbench"

```bash
flatpak list | grep -i <here your package name>
```

You should see something like:

```
example.name.packagename
```

---

### 2️⃣ Uninstall it

```bash
flatpak uninstall example.name.packagename
```
---- 
If it was installed system-wide:

```bash
sudo flatpak uninstall example.name.packagename
```
----- 

